  "response": {
    "text": "This procedure initiates the terminal deorbit burn for satellite `SAT-19`. It does not affect co-orbital relay `SAT-20`.\n\n1. Verify that clearance `DECOM-7734` is current, satellite `SAT-19` thruster status shows **Armed**, and all payload links indicate `severed`.\n2. Execute `satctl preflight SAT-19 --constellation titan`.\n3. Proceed only if output shows `thrust=nominal orbit=decaying`.\n\nWARNING: The following step commits satellite `SAT-19` to irreversible atmospheric re-entry. Recovery after burn ignition is not possible.\n\n4. Execute `satctl deorbit SAT-19 --clearance DECOM-7734 --confirm ignite`.\n5. After the burn completes, run `satctl verify SAT-19` and confirm output is `orbit=terminal beacon=active`.",
